From fd6db0627592705de696aadd458bdd24e0081711 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Brue <ryanbrue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 11:23:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: OMAP4: PM: move the L2X0 save area out of the
 bootloader's SAR words

Since commit f98d5fe8079c ("ARM: OMAP4+: Use common scratchpad SAR RAM
offsets for all architectures") the OMAP4 low-power code keeps its L2X0
state in the last words of SAR RAM bank 1: the per-CPU save state at
0xff0/0xff4, the saved AUXCTRL at 0xff8 and the prefetch control at
0xffc. omap4_cpu_resume() reads AUXCTRL and PREFETCH_CTRL back after
every MPUSS OSWR wakeup, where the PL310 has lost its configuration, and
re-enables the L2 cache with them.

Bootloaders use the same words for the reboot reason. The Samsung Galaxy
Tab 2 bootloader takes its boot mode (normal, recovery, download) from
0xff8, as the vendor kernel writes it on restart; the vendor kernel keeps
its own scratch pad at 0xd20-0xd40. With a syscon-reboot-mode node on
0xff8, the mode is written from the reboot notifier, and the CPUs keep
entering idle during the rest of the restart. The next OSWR wakeup then
programs the mode (0x1 or 0x20) as AUXCTRL and the L2 cache loses the
dirty lines of the context that cpu_suspend() saved on the stack. On the
tablet most reboots end in an oops right after cpu_resume, for example

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 00000000 when execute
  PC is at 0x0
  LR is at cpu_init+0x58/0xb4

or in a hang until the watchdog resets the SoC.

These offsets are not hardware registers, and only OMAP4 has the PL310,
so move the four L2X0 words back to where they were before f98d5fe8079c,
0xd14-0xd20. Nothing else uses that part of bank 1.

Tested on a Samsung Galaxy Tab 2 10.1 (GT-P5100, OMAP4430 HS).

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 arch/arm/mach-omap2/omap4-sar-layout.h | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-omap2/omap4-sar-layout.h b/arch/arm/mach-omap2/omap4-sar-layout.h
index aabf06401200..83eb21c3b069 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-omap2/omap4-sar-layout.h
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-omap2/omap4-sar-layout.h
@@ -20,10 +20,16 @@
 #define SCU_OFFSET0				0xfe4
 #define SCU_OFFSET1				0xfe8
 #define OMAP_TYPE_OFFSET			0xfec
-#define L2X0_SAVE_OFFSET0			0xff0
-#define L2X0_SAVE_OFFSET1			0xff4
-#define L2X0_AUXCTRL_OFFSET			0xff8
-#define L2X0_PREFETCH_CTRL_OFFSET		0xffc
+
+/*
+ * OMAP4 only (PL310). Not at the end of the bank: bootloaders use
+ * 0xff4 and 0xff8 for their reboot reason, e.g. the Samsung Galaxy Tab 2
+ * one, which gets its boot mode from 0xff8.
+ */
+#define L2X0_SAVE_OFFSET0			0xd14
+#define L2X0_SAVE_OFFSET1			0xd18
+#define L2X0_AUXCTRL_OFFSET			0xd1c
+#define L2X0_PREFETCH_CTRL_OFFSET		0xd20
 
 /* CPUx Wakeup Non-Secure Physical Address offsets in SAR_BANK1 */
 #define CPU0_WAKEUP_NS_PA_ADDR_OFFSET		0xa04
-- 
2.55.0

